metaflac: print --version through flac_printf.

metaflac puts stdout in _O_U8TEXT whenever it converts tags to UTF-8, which is
the default; in that mode the narrow printf writes nothing. Every other line it
prints goes through flac_printf (= printf_utf8 on Windows); show_version() did
not, so on Windows `metaflac --version` printed an empty line and exited 0.
Off Windows flac_printf is printf.

Upstream xiph/flac 018b4ac (#812), after 1.5.0. Drop this patch when the flac
release that carries it reaches nixpkgs.

--- a/src/metaflac/operations.c
+++ b/src/metaflac/operations.c
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@
 
 void show_version(void)
 {
-	printf("metaflac %s\n", FLAC__VERSION_STRING);
+	flac_printf("metaflac %s\n", FLAC__VERSION_STRING);
 }
 
 FLAC__bool do_major_operation(const CommandLineOptions *options)
